ss="object-cover w-full hidden md:block z-1" role="presentation"/><div role="presentation" class="absolute inset-0 -z-2 bg-gradient-to-t from-[rgba(28,30,32,1)] to-[rgba(28,30,32,0.5)]"></div></div></section><div class="relative"><div aria-hidden="true" class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none"></div><section class="py-10 md:py-20 light:bg-white container max-w-3xl"><header class="max-w-9xl mx-auto px-4 text-center flex flex-col items-center gap-4 [&amp;_mark]:bg-transparent! [&amp;_mark]:text-font-brand! [&amp;_br]:hidden md:[&amp;_br]:block mb-8 md:mb-15"><h2 itemProp="name" class="font-grotesk text-brand-h-sm font-bold uppercase whitespace-pre-wrap px-5 text-font-primary light:text-font-primary-reverted md:text-brand-h-lg">Still have questions?</h2><p itemProp="description" class="text-caption-l text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-wrap">We’ve answered the most frequently asked questions</p></header><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">What is Google Veo 3.1?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Veo 3.1 is latest AI video generation model by Google, that creates high-quality videos in 1080p from simple text prompts or reference images. It offers a new level of creative control through three powerful generation modes.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">What is the difference between the &#x27;Standard&#x27; and &#x27;Fast&#x27; models?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Standard model uses Reference-to-Video for keeping subjects consistent and ideal for complex scenes, while Fast uses Start &amp; End Frame for controlling motion and has faster generation time.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">What is the maximum video length I can generate using Veo 3.1?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">You can generate videos with a selectable duration of 4 seconds, 6 seconds, or 8 seconds.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">What video formats and resolutions are supported?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Veo 3.1 supports both 720p and 1080p resolutions at 24 FPS. You can generate videos with durations of 4, 6, or 8 seconds in either 16:9 (landscape) or 9:16 (portrait) aspect ratios.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">What is Subject Consistency?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Exclusive to the Standard model, this feature allows you to upload 1-3 reference images of a character or object. The AI then maintains the subject&#x27;s identity and appearance across all frames of the video, ensuring perfect continuity.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">Does Veo 3.1 support dialogues?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Yes, the Standard model supports speaking characters with realistic facial expressions and lip-syncing, making it perfect for storytelling, marketing content, or any video featuring dialogue.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">What aspect ratios are supported?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">You can create videos in the two most popular aspect ratios. 16:9 (Landscape), perfect for cinematic shots, YouTube, and standard television formats and 9:16 (Portrait), ideal for mobile-first platforms like TikTok, Instagram Reels, and YouTube Shorts.</div></details></section></div><section class="py-10 md:py-20 container max-w-8xl relative"><div aria-hidden="true" class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none"></div><h2 class="text-brand-h-sm font-bold text-center mb-8 uppercase font-grotesk md:text-brand-h-lg">Explore more AI features</h2><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 justify-center"><a href="/ai-video" class="h-8 rounded-full md:rounded-lg inline-grid items-center text-font-secondary bg-surface-primary font-medium px-3">AI Video Generator</a><a href="/sora-2" class="h-8 rounded-full md:rounded-lg inline-grid items-center text-font-secondary bg-surface-primary font-medium px-3">Sora 2</a><a href="/kling-3.0" class="h-8 rounded-full md:rounded-lg inline-grid items-center text-font-secondary bg-surface-primary font-medium px-3">Kling 3.0</a><a href="/sora-2-upscale" class="h-8 rounded-full md:rounded-lg inline-gri